config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_ZIGBEE2MQTT
	bool "Domoticz plugin: Zigbee2MQTT"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_REQUESTS
	default n
	help
		expose the Zigbee devices managed by Zigbee2MQTT in Domoticz, with adapters for hundreds of models and a configuration frontend (it ships its own model adapters and talks to Zigbee2MQTT through an MQTT broker).

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/zigbee2mqtt, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		Setup -> Hardware -> Zigbee2MQTT, enter the address and port of the MQTT broker used by Zigbee2MQTT.

		Licensed upstream (LICENSE is installed with the plugin). The
		repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a pinned commit of
		the default branch.
